    faq: [
      { q: "How do I calculate concrete for a hollow tube?", a: "The calculator subtracts the inner-circle area from the outer-circle area, multiplies by height and quantity, then converts to cubic yards." },
      { q: "Can I enter wall thickness instead of inside diameter?", a: "Yes. When inside diameter is zero and wall thickness is provided, the calculator derives the inside diameter from the outside diameter." },
      { q: "What happens if wall thickness is too large?", a: "The calculator rejects a wall thickness equal to or greater than half the outside diameter because that would eliminate the hollow opening." },
